What this command does
nano

nano is a simple text editor in Linux.

It allows you to:

Create a new file
Open an existing file
Edit file contents
~/enterprise-ai-platform/api/main.py
~ = Home directory of the current user
enterprise-ai-platform = Project folder
api = Subfolder
main.py = Python file

So the command means:

Open the file main.py inside the api folder using the Nano editor. If the file does not exist, create it.

Execute
Shell
nano ~/enterprise-ai-platform/api/main.py
 

After pressing Enter, Nano editor opens.

Add Python Code

For example:
------------------------
main.py 


from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {"message": "Enterprise AI Platform Running"}






------------------------


